cluewren contains material derived from Aura Autopilot
(https://github.com/ramenvr/autopilot, commit 48966d1), Copyright its authors, licensed under
the Apache License 2.0.

Derived:

- the bridge protocol;
- src/Cluewren.Kit: a port of autopilot/kit (game, control, nav, geom, harness),
  autopilot/runtime.py, the Unity adapter in autopilot/engines (base.py, unity.py) and the live-game
  helpers of autopilot/research.py, with their tuned constants, the Jev decision rules, the default
  instructions and the text of summaries and check reports;
- src/Cluewren/Sandbox: a port of the split in autopilot/sandbox.py and of the tool bodies
  in autopilot/agents/session.py (probe, run_harness, snapshot, restart_level);
- docs/KIT.md, KIT-UNITY.md, KIT-GODOT.md and KIT-UNREAL.md: a port of autopilot/KIT.md and of
  autopilot/engines/unity.md and godot.md;
- tests/Cluewren.Tests: ports of upstream's kit and runtime tests and of its simulated game
  (tests/conftest.py, tests/navsim.py and others);
- the plugins under plugin/unity, plugin/godot and plugin/unreal, each with its own NOTICE.

The ported files were changed from the Python originals: rewritten in C#, with async executors, a
sandbox host of its own, and without Autopilot's upload, sign-in and billing code.
